   "headline": "Heat Advisory issued October 16 at 7:50PM PDT until October 17 at 8:00PM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
   "description": "* WHAT...Temperatures up to 95 expected.\n\n* WHERE...Coastal areas of southwest California\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM PDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hot temperatures may cause heat illnesses.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Weaker winds tonight and Saturday.",
   "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids, stay in an air-conditioned room, stay out of\nthe sun, and check up on relatives and neighbors.\n\nIn the event of a nearby wildfire, smoke may increase heat and\nphysical stress. If smoke impacts your area; 1) Have a cooling plan\nin place as smoke could limit your ability to cool your home through\nopen windows and 2) If you have air conditioning, set on air\nrecirculation within the home to avoid smoke exposure. Local\nofficials may have additional guidance.",
